1
00:00:00,640 --> 00:00:03,600
Hi,  and  welcome  back  to  act.  You

2
00:00:03,600 --> 00:00:05,920
have  one  solution  now.  The  next

3
00:00:05,920 --> 00:00:07,480
step  is  to  make  it  clear  enough

4
00:00:07,480 --> 00:00:09,360
that  someone  can  understand  what

5
00:00:09,360 --> 00:00:11,920
you  actually  want  to  do.

6
00:00:11,920 --> 00:00:13,519
A  useful  way  to  check  that  is

7
00:00:13,519 --> 00:00:15,839
the  smart  model.  Smart  gives  us

8
00:00:15,839 --> 00:00:18,800
five  simple  checks,  specific,

9
00:00:18,800 --> 00:00:21,800
measurable,  attainable,  relevant,

10
00:00:21,800 --> 00:00:23,119
and  timely.

11
00:00:23,119 --> 00:00:24,800
You  do  not  need  to  memorize  big

12
00:00:24,800 --> 00:00:26,760
definitions.  We  are  going  to  take

13
00:00:26,760 --> 00:00:28,199
the  solution  you  chose  and  make

14
00:00:28,199 --> 00:00:30,759
it  clearer  one  part  at  a  time.

15
00:00:30,759 --> 00:00:32,200
By  the  end,  you  should  be  able

16
00:00:32,200 --> 00:00:34,160
to  explain  what  you  want  to  do,

17
00:00:34,160 --> 00:00:36,320
who  it  is  for,  what  success  could

18
00:00:36,320 --> 00:00:38,120
look  like,  whether  it  can  really

19
00:00:38,120 --> 00:00:39,760
be  done  and  when  it  should

20
00:00:39,760 --> 00:00:40,416
happen.

21
00:00:40,656 --> 00:00:44,095
specific.  A  vague  idea  like  raise

22
00:00:44,095 --> 00:00:46,096
awareness  about  smoking  does  not

23
00:00:46,096 --> 00:00:48,016
tell  us  enough.  What  kind  of

24
00:00:48,016 --> 00:00:50,935
awareness?  For  whom?  Where?  And

25
00:00:50,935 --> 00:00:53,256
what  exactly  will  you  do?

26
00:00:53,256 --> 00:00:55,536
A  more  specific  version  could  be

27
00:00:55,536 --> 00:00:57,256
run  awareness  sessions  about  the

28
00:00:57,256 --> 00:00:58,936
harmful  effects  of  smoking  for

29
00:00:58,936 --> 00:01:01,296
high  school  students  in  one  city.

30
00:01:01,296 --> 00:01:03,136
Now  we  can  picture  the  action,

31
00:01:03,136 --> 00:01:04,976
the  topic,  the  people,  and  the

32
00:01:04,976 --> 00:01:06,096
place.

33
00:01:06,096 --> 00:01:07,296
Do  the  same  with  your  own

34
00:01:07,296 --> 00:01:09,896
solution.  Ask  yourself,  what  do  I

35
00:01:09,896 --> 00:01:11,695
want  to  achieve,  why  does  it

36
00:01:11,695 --> 00:01:14,376
matter?  How  might  I  do  it?  Who

37
00:01:14,376 --> 00:01:16,176
is  involved?  And  where  will  it

38
00:01:16,176 --> 00:01:17,295
happen?

39
00:01:17,295 --> 00:01:19,416
You  do  not  need  every  detail  yet,

40
00:01:19,416 --> 00:01:21,582
but  the  direction  should  be  clear.

41
00:01:21,822 --> 00:01:24,461
M  stands  for  measurable.  This

42
00:01:24,461 --> 00:01:25,941
means  adding  something  you  can

43
00:01:25,941 --> 00:01:27,742
count  or  check  so  you  know

44
00:01:27,742 --> 00:01:29,542
whether  the  goal  was  reached.

45
00:01:29,542 --> 00:01:31,261
Using  the  same  example,  we  could

46
00:01:31,261 --> 00:01:33,982
say  run  three  awareness  sessions

47
00:01:33,982 --> 00:01:36,822
for  200  high  school  students.  Now,

48
00:01:36,822 --> 00:01:38,822
there's  something  clear  to  measure.

49
00:01:38,822 --> 00:01:40,941
Three  sessions  and  200  people

50
00:01:40,941 --> 00:01:42,982
reached.  Your  number  will  depend

51
00:01:42,982 --> 00:01:45,021
on  your  own  project.  It  might  be

52
00:01:45,021 --> 00:01:47,502
people  reached,  sessions  completed,

53
00:01:47,502 --> 00:01:49,941
items  delivered,  responses  collected

54
00:01:49,941 --> 00:01:51,621
or  another  simple  measure  that

55
00:01:51,621 --> 00:01:53,422
It's  the  solution.  The  point  is

56
00:01:53,422 --> 00:01:55,661
not  to  chase  a  big  number.  The

57
00:01:55,661 --> 00:01:57,141
point  is  to  know  what  you  will

58
00:01:57,141 --> 00:01:59,102
look  at  later  when  you  ask,  "Did

59
00:01:59,102 --> 00:02:01,332
we  actually  do  what  we  planned?"

60
00:02:01,332 --> 00:02:04,531
A  stands  for  attainable.  You

61
00:02:04,531 --> 00:02:06,052
already  checked  part  of  this  when

62
00:02:06,052 --> 00:02:08,171
you  used  the  solution  filter.

63
00:02:08,171 --> 00:02:10,092
Can  this  idea  really  be  done  with

64
00:02:10,092 --> 00:02:12,332
your  current  ability,  limits  and

65
00:02:12,332 --> 00:02:14,332
available  support?

66
00:02:14,332 --> 00:02:16,692
R  stands  for  relevant  here,

67
00:02:16,692 --> 00:02:18,292
meaning  the  goal  should  also  be

68
00:02:18,292 --> 00:02:20,052
realistic  and  workable  in  the

69
00:02:20,052 --> 00:02:21,371
situation.

70
00:02:21,371 --> 00:02:23,172
If  there  are  only  500  people  in

71
00:02:23,172 --> 00:02:24,172
the  group  you  are  trying  to

72
00:02:24,172 --> 00:02:27,212
reach,  planning  for  5,000  does  not

73
00:02:27,212 --> 00:02:28,371
make  sense.

74
00:02:28,371 --> 00:02:30,652
The  same  goes  for  money,  access,

75
00:02:30,652 --> 00:02:32,691
time  or  other  limits.

76
00:02:32,691 --> 00:02:34,452
A  strong  goal  should  stretch  you

77
00:02:34,452 --> 00:02:36,252
a  little,  but  it  should  still

78
00:02:36,252 --> 00:02:38,092
live  in  the  real  world.

79
00:02:38,092 --> 00:02:40,492
If  something  clearly  cannot  work,

80
00:02:40,492 --> 00:02:42,211
adjust  the  size  or  the  way  you

81
00:02:42,211 --> 00:02:43,332
plan  to  do  it.

82
00:02:43,572 --> 00:02:46,292
T  stands  for  timely.  Give  the

83
00:02:46,292 --> 00:02:49,292
solution  a  clear  time  or  period.

84
00:02:49,292 --> 00:02:51,171
When  will  you  start  and  by  when

85
00:02:51,171 --> 00:02:53,212
should  the  action  be  completed?

86
00:02:53,212 --> 00:02:55,492
The  awareness  example  could  become

87
00:02:55,492 --> 00:02:57,492
run  three  awareness  sessions  for

88
00:02:57,492 --> 00:02:59,332
200  high  school  students  during

89
00:02:59,332 --> 00:03:01,572
the  first  semester.  Now  the  action

90
00:03:01,572 --> 00:03:03,531
has  a  time  frame.  Your  own

91
00:03:03,531 --> 00:03:06,052
project  may  use  a  week,  a  month,

92
00:03:06,052 --> 00:03:08,652
a  semester,  a  campaign  period  or

93
00:03:08,652 --> 00:03:10,292
another  clear  window.

94
00:03:10,292 --> 00:03:12,252
Time  matters  because  it  helps  you

95
00:03:12,252 --> 00:03:14,212
know  how  fast  you need  to  move,

96
00:03:14,212 --> 00:03:15,492
and  whether  the  goal  is  still

97
00:03:15,492 --> 00:03:16,731
realistic.

98
00:03:16,731 --> 00:03:18,652
Without  a  time  frame,  it  is  very

99
00:03:18,652 --> 00:03:20,492
easy  for  a  good  idea  to  keep

100
00:03:20,492 --> 00:03:22,372
getting  pushed  into  later  without

101
00:03:22,372 --> 00:03:23,623
ever  becoming  real.

102
00:03:23,903 --> 00:03:25,903
Now  take  your  final  solution  and

103
00:03:25,903 --> 00:03:28,063
rewrite  it  using  all  five  smart

104
00:03:28,063 --> 00:03:29,063
checks.

105
00:03:29,063 --> 00:03:30,902
Ask  yourself,  is  it  specific

106
00:03:30,902 --> 00:03:32,063
enough  that  someone  else

107
00:03:32,063 --> 00:03:34,063
understands  it?  Can  I  measure

108
00:03:34,063 --> 00:03:35,743
something  important?  Is  it

109
00:03:35,743 --> 00:03:37,503
attainable  with  what  I  have  or

110
00:03:37,503 --> 00:03:39,462
can  reasonably  get?  Is  it

111
00:03:39,462 --> 00:03:41,623
realistic  for  this  situation?  And

112
00:03:41,623 --> 00:03:43,463
is  the  time  clear?

113
00:03:43,463 --> 00:03:45,303
If  one  part  is  weak,  change  the

114
00:03:45,303 --> 00:03:46,303
sentence.

115
00:03:46,303 --> 00:03:47,742
Do  not  worry  if  your  first

116
00:03:47,742 --> 00:03:49,822
version  feels  messy.  The  point  of

117
00:03:49,822 --> 00:03:51,863
smart  is  to  turn  a  broad  idea

118
00:03:51,863 --> 00:03:53,302
into  something  you  can  actually

119
00:03:53,302 --> 00:03:54,503
work with.

120
00:03:54,503 --> 00:03:56,062
Keep  improving  the  wording  until

121
00:03:56,062 --> 00:03:58,303
the  solution  feels  clear,  possible

122
00:03:58,303 --> 00:03:59,783
and  connected  to  the  need  you've

123
00:03:59,783 --> 00:04:01,414
been  carrying  through  this  unit.

124
00:04:01,414 --> 00:04:03,694
Once  the  solution  is  clear,  you

125
00:04:03,694 --> 00:04:05,934
can  ask  another  question.  Is  there

126
00:04:05,934 --> 00:04:07,894
a  better  or  more  creative  way  to

127
00:04:07,894 --> 00:04:08,894
do  it?

128
00:04:08,894 --> 00:04:10,814
Innovation  does  not  always  mean

129
00:04:10,814 --> 00:04:13,013
expensive  technology  or  something

130
00:04:13,013 --> 00:04:15,053
nobody  has  ever  seen  before.

131
00:04:15,053 --> 00:04:16,894
Sometimes  it  simply  means  looking

132
00:04:16,894 --> 00:04:18,734
at  the  same  idea  from  a  different

133
00:04:18,734 --> 00:04:20,654
angle  and  finding  a  fresh  way  to

134
00:04:20,654 --> 00:04:22,094
make  it  work.

135
00:04:22,094 --> 00:04:23,894
Imagine  giving  five  people  the

136
00:04:23,894 --> 00:04:26,654
same  unfinished  drawing.  One  person

137
00:04:26,654 --> 00:04:28,654
may  see  a  face,  another  may  see

138
00:04:28,654 --> 00:04:30,693
a  road,  and  someone  else  may  turn

139
00:04:30,693 --> 00:04:32,134
it  into  something completely

140
00:04:32,134 --> 00:04:34,054
different.  The  starting  point  is

141
00:04:34,054 --> 00:04:35,934
the  same,  but  the  way  they  look

142
00:04:35,934 --> 00:04:38,254
at  it  changes  the  result.  You  can

143
00:04:38,254 --> 00:04:39,653
do  the  same  with  a  community

144
00:04:39,653 --> 00:04:40,705
solution.

145
00:04:40,705 --> 00:04:43,545
Try  a  small  creativity  exercise.

146
00:04:43,545 --> 00:04:45,145
Write  your  solution  in  the  middle

147
00:04:45,145 --> 00:04:47,464
of  a  page.  Around  it,  add  a  few

148
00:04:47,464 --> 00:04:49,905
random  prompts  such  as  location,

149
00:04:49,905 --> 00:04:52,945
time,  audience,  partner,  social

150
00:04:52,945 --> 00:04:57,105
media,  mobile,  book,  game,  color,

151
00:04:57,105 --> 00:04:59,064
or  another  simple  word.

152
00:04:59,064 --> 00:05:01,585
Pick  three  prompts  and  ask,  could

153
00:05:01,585 --> 00:05:03,425
this  change  the  way  I  deliver  the

154
00:05:03,425 --> 00:05:04,545
solution?

155
00:05:04,545 --> 00:05:06,665
Maybe  the  location  changes.  Maybe

156
00:05:06,665 --> 00:05:08,025
the  way  people  hear  about  it

157
00:05:08,025 --> 00:05:10,185
changes.  Maybe  a  partner  makes  it

158
00:05:10,185 --> 00:05:11,505
easier  to  Reach  the  people  who

159
00:05:11,505 --> 00:05:12,505
need  it.

160
00:05:12,505 --> 00:05:14,145
You  do  not  have  to  use  every

161
00:05:14,145 --> 00:05:16,424
idea.  The  goal  is  simply  to  break

162
00:05:16,424 --> 00:05:17,865
your  normal  pattern  for  a  few

163
00:05:17,865 --> 00:05:19,545
minutes  and  see  whether  a  fresh

164
00:05:19,545 --> 00:05:21,455
angle  gives  you  something  useful.

165
00:05:21,455 --> 00:05:23,455
Now,  look  at  the  ideas  you

166
00:05:23,455 --> 00:05:26,055
created.  Keep  the  useful  parts,

167
00:05:26,055 --> 00:05:27,895
combine  ideas  that  work  well

168
00:05:27,895 --> 00:05:30,134
together  and  remove  anything  that

169
00:05:30,134 --> 00:05:32,174
makes  the  solution  weaker  or  more

170
00:05:32,174 --> 00:05:33,575
confusing.

171
00:05:33,575 --> 00:05:36,014
A  creative  idea  is  only  helpful

172
00:05:36,014 --> 00:05:38,455
if  it  still  fits  the  real  need

173
00:05:38,455 --> 00:05:40,415
and  can  actually  work.

174
00:05:40,415 --> 00:05:41,894
If  your  new  version  changes

175
00:05:41,894 --> 00:05:43,695
something  important,  like  who  you

176
00:05:43,695 --> 00:05:45,974
are  helping,  how  much  you  will  do

177
00:05:45,974 --> 00:05:47,935
or  when  it  will  happen,  update

178
00:05:47,935 --> 00:05:49,894
your  smart  statement  too.

179
00:05:49,894 --> 00:05:51,974
You  are  not  adding  creativity just

180
00:05:51,974 --> 00:05:53,975
to  make  the  project  look  special.

181
00:05:53,975 --> 00:05:55,455
You  are  trying  to  make  the  final

182
00:05:55,455 --> 00:05:57,975
solution  clearer,  stronger,  more

183
00:05:57,975 --> 00:06:00,615
original  or  easier  to  use  while

184
00:06:00,615 --> 00:06:02,621
still  keeping  it  realistic.

185
00:06:02,621 --> 00:06:04,541
One  more  thing  before  we  close  the

186
00:06:04,541 --> 00:06:07,301
unit.  Your  action  can  affect  more

187
00:06:07,301 --> 00:06:09,301
people  than  you  expect.

188
00:06:09,301 --> 00:06:10,821
Think  about  a  row  of  connected

189
00:06:10,821 --> 00:06:13,501
pieces.  Move  one  and  the  movement

190
00:06:13,501 --> 00:06:15,300
can  reach  the  next  one,  then  the

191
00:06:15,300 --> 00:06:16,621
next.

192
00:06:16,621 --> 00:06:18,941
Community  work  can  be  similar.

193
00:06:18,941 --> 00:06:21,021
A  useful  action  may  directly  help

194
00:06:21,021 --> 00:06:23,781
one  group,  then  influence  families,

195
00:06:23,781 --> 00:06:25,980
co-workers,  neighbors  or  other

196
00:06:25,980 --> 00:06:27,581
people  around  them.

197
00:06:27,581 --> 00:06:29,300
Some  effects  may  happen  even  when

198
00:06:29,300 --> 00:06:31,181
you  did  not  plan  them.

199
00:06:31,181 --> 00:06:32,660
That  is  why  it  is  worth  thinking

200
00:06:32,660 --> 00:06:34,981
beyond  the  first  result.

201
00:06:34,981 --> 00:06:37,061
Ask  yourself,  if  this  solution

202
00:06:37,061 --> 00:06:39,061
works,  who  else  could  be  affected

203
00:06:39,061 --> 00:06:40,020
by  it?

204
00:06:40,020 --> 00:06:42,020
What  good  change  might  spread  from

205
00:06:42,020 --> 00:06:43,660
the  first  action?

206
00:06:43,660 --> 00:06:45,020
This  helps  you  see  the  wider

207
00:06:45,020 --> 00:06:46,621
meaning  of  what  you  are  building.

208
00:06:46,621 --> 00:06:49,901
That's  the  end  of  unit  three.

209
00:06:49,901 --> 00:06:52,500
Look  at  how  far  one  idea  has

210
00:06:52,500 --> 00:06:54,941
traveled.  You  chose  a  real

211
00:06:54,941 --> 00:06:57,821
problem,  understood  the  need  behind

212
00:06:57,821 --> 00:07:00,140
it,  created  several  possible

213
00:07:00,140 --> 00:07:03,061
solutions,  compared  them,  selected

214
00:07:03,061 --> 00:07:05,701
one,  made  it  smart,  and  looked

215
00:07:05,701 --> 00:07:08,701
for  a  stronger  way  to  deliver  it.

216
00:07:08,701 --> 00:07:11,301
Keep  that  final  solution  safe

217
00:07:11,301 --> 00:07:13,101
because  unit  four  starts  from

218
00:07:13,101 --> 00:07:14,980
exactly  there.

219
00:07:14,980 --> 00:07:17,060
The  question  changes  from  What

220
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:19,541
should  I  do?  To  how  will  I

221
00:07:19,541 --> 00:07:22,020
actually  make  this  hacking?

222
00:07:22,020 --> 00:07:24,461
Next,  we  move  into  planning,  then

223
00:07:24,461 --> 00:07:27,061
execution  and  finally  sharing  what

224
00:07:27,061 --> 00:07:28,261
happened.

225
00:07:28,261 --> 00:07:30,660
Your  idea  is  ready  to  become  a

226
00:07:30,660 --> 00:07:32,381
real  plan.

227
00:07:32,381 --> 00:07:33,981
Keep  your  work  with  you  and  I'll

